# Database URL — use PostgreSQL for serverless deployment (Vercel/Netlify).
# SQLite doesn't work on serverless because the filesystem is read-only.
#
# === OPTION 1: Vercel Postgres (recommended for Vercel) ===
# 1. Go to your Vercel project → Storage → Create → Postgres
# 2. Copy the connection string (starts with postgres://)
# 3. Set it as an environment variable named DATABASE_URL in Vercel
#
# === OPTION 2: Neon (free, works anywhere) ===
# 1. Go to https://neon.tech → Create account → Create project
# 2. Copy the connection string
# 3. Set as DATABASE_URL environment variable
#
# === OPTION 3: Supabase (free, works anywhere) ===
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com → Create project
# 2. Settings → Database → Connection string → URI
# 3. Set as DATABASE_URL environment variable
#
# For LOCAL DEVELOPMENT with SQLite (offline), uncomment the line below:
# DATABASE_URL=file:./db/custom.db
#
# For LOCAL DEVELOPMENT with PostgreSQL, use your external DB URL:
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname?sslmode=require
